1
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:14,020
Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,620
Welcome back to Business English Learning.

3
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:21,620
Hi, everyone. Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice. I'm Daniel.

4
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:28,320
And I'm Sophia, and we're here to help you speak English naturally and confidently in real-life situations.

5
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:34,520
Today we have a very practical and powerful topic, how to get promoted at work.

6
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:39,680
Yes, this is something many people want, but not everyone knows how to talk about it clearly

7
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:43,200
in English or even how to approach it in real life.

8
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,700
Exactly.

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,760
Getting promoted is not just about working hard.

10
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:54,400
It's also about communication, visibility, mindset and knowing how to express your value.

11
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:59,280
And today we're going to guide you through all of that using natural conversation, real

12
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:04,160
life examples and useful phrases you can actually use at work.

13
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:09,160
We'll talk about what it means to get promoted, how to show you're ready, how to talk to your

14
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:13,520
manager and even what to do if you don't get promoted right away.

15
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:18,280
So if you want to grow in your career and speak about it confidently in English, you're

16
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:19,960
in the right place.

17
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:23,240
Alright Sophia, are you ready to get promoted in English?

18
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:25,320
I've been ready since last year.

19
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,520
Let's get started.

20
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,360
So Sophia, how are you today?

21
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,360
I'm doing well.

22
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,080
I feel productive today.

23
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:36,520
I planned my week, organized my tasks, and even started working on a new project early.

24
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,520
How about you?

25
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:40,480
I'm doing okay, but I had a funny moment this morning.

26
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:41,920
Oh, what happened?

27
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:47,400
I looked at my to-do list and wrote, Today I will be extremely productive.

28
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,000
That sounds like a strong start.

29
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,720
Yes, but then I spent 20 minutes choosing which coffee to make.

30
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:56,400
That is also a very important decision.

31
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,040
Of course.

32
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,200
Productivity starts with good coffee.

33
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:05,880
Absolutely. So speaking of productivity, do you think being productive helps people get promoted?

34
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:11,800
Definitely. Productivity is one of the key factors, but it's not just about working more.

35
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:14,940
It's about working smarter and showing results.

36
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:20,320
That's interesting because many people think if I just work harder, I will get promoted.

37
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:26,560
Yes, but that's not always enough. You also need visibility, communication and initiative.

38
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:31,760
Initiative is a great word. It means doing things without being told, right?

39
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:37,480
Exactly. For example, if you see a problem and you fix it without waiting for instructions,

40
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:38,960
that shows initiative.

41
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:44,640
So, if someone wants to get promoted, they should not just do their tasks, but also go

42
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,400
beyond them.

43
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:49,400
Yes, they should show that they can handle more responsibility.

44
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:56,040
Responsibility is another keyword. When you get promoted, you usually take on more responsibility.

45
00:02:56,040 --> 00:03:03,040
Right. A promotion means your role changes. You may manage people, lead projects, or make decisions.

46
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:09,040
Let's start simple. If someone asks, what does it mean to get promoted, how can we answer?

47
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:15,040
A simple answer is, getting promoted means moving to a higher position with more responsibility,

48
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:18,040
a better title, and often higher pay.

49
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:24,040
That's clear. So if I say, I got promoted last month, what can I add to make it stronger?

50
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,040
You can explain your old role, your new role, and what changed.

51
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:31,040
For example, I got promoted last month.

52
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:34,040
I was a junior analyst, and now I'm a senior analyst.

53
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:37,040
I also lead a small team now.

54
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:40,040
Perfect. That's clear, professional, and informative.

55
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:43,040
Now let's talk about something important.

56
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:46,040
How do people actually get promoted?

57
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:49,040
Good question. There are several key factors.

58
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:53,040
Performance, consistency, communication, and attitude.

59
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:58,040
Let's break that down. Performance means how well you do your job, right?

60
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:06,040
Yes. If you consistently deliver high-quality work, meet deadlines, and solve problems, your performance is strong.

61
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:13,040
Consistently is an important word. It means doing something well again and again, not just once.

62
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:17,040
Exactly. Managers look for people who are reliable over time.

63
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:21,120
So, if I finish one project well, that's good.

64
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:24,400
But if I finish many projects well, that's better.

65
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,400
Much better.

66
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:27,300
That shows consistency.

67
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,480
What about communication?

68
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:30,840
Communication is critical.

69
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:35,320
You need to share updates, ask questions, and express ideas clearly.

70
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:39,720
So, if I do great work but never speak up, that could be a problem.

71
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:42,600
Yes, people need to know what you're doing.

72
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,680
That's interesting.

73
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:47,600
So it's not about showing off, but about keeping people informed.

74
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,760
Exactly.

75
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:53,400
You can say things like, I'd like to update you on the project, or here's what I've

76
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,900
completed this week.

77
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,920
Let's talk about initiative again.

78
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,400
Can you give a real example?

79
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,400
Sure.

80
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:03,320
Imagine your team is struggling with a process that takes too long.

81
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:08,200
If you suggest a new system and help implement it, that shows initiative.

82
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:11,680
So instead of waiting for instructions, you take action.

83
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,900
Yes, and that makes managers think,

84
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:16,840
this person is ready for more responsibility.

85
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,720
That's exactly what you need for a promotion.

86
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:22,600
Now let's talk about a very important situation,

87
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:25,520
talking to your manager about getting promoted.

88
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:28,520
Yes, many people feel nervous about this.

89
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,720
That's true, but it's actually a normal

90
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,600
and professional conversation.

91
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,760
So how can someone start?

92
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,560
They can say, I'd like to talk

93
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,400
about my career development.

94
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,120
That sounds very professional.

95
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:45,040
Or, I'm interested in growing in the company and taking on more responsibility.

96
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:48,560
That sounds much better than, I want a promotion now.

97
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,960
Exactly.

98
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,800
Tone is very important.

99
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:55,560
Tone means the feeling or attitude in your words, right?

100
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,560
Yes.

101
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,240
You want to sound confident but not demanding.

102
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,320
Let me try a full example.

103
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,320
Go ahead.

104
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:06,480
I really enjoy my current role and I'm interested in growing in the company.

105
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:10,480
I'd like to understand what I need to do to move to the next level.

106
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:14,980
That's excellent. It shows interest, respect, and motivation.

107
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:17,480
And it also invites feedback.

108
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:21,480
Exactly. Speaking of feedback, why is it important?

109
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:26,480
Feedback helps you understand what you're doing well and what you need to improve.

110
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:31,480
So, if I want a promotion, I should ask, can you give me feedback on my performance?

111
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:35,980
Yes, or what skills should I develop to move to the next level?

112
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,620
That shows you are serious about growth.

113
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:40,820
Now let's talk about preparation.

114
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:44,060
Before asking for a promotion, what should you do?

115
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:47,460
You should prepare examples of your work and achievements.

116
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:48,620
Exactly.

117
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:52,420
Don't just say, I work hard, show specific results.

118
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:55,820
For example, I completed three major projects,

119
00:06:55,820 --> 00:06:57,740
helped train new team members,

120
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:00,340
and improved our process efficiency.

121
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:03,500
Perfect. That's strong and convincing.

122
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,580
Now let's talk about mindset.

123
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:08,380
How should someone think if they want to get promoted?

124
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:11,380
They should think like someone at the next level.

125
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:12,580
What does that mean?

126
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:16,880
It means acting like the role you want, not just the role you have.

127
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:22,380
So if I want to be a team leader, I should start helping others and organizing tasks.

128
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:26,080
Exactly. Show leadership before you get the title.

129
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,580
That's powerful.

130
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:30,180
Now let's talk about a difficult situation.

131
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,380
What if someone doesn't get promoted?

132
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:36,380
That happens often, and it's important to respond professionally.

133
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:37,380
What can they say?

134
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:43,380
They can say, I'm disappointed, but I'd like to understand how I can improve for next time.

135
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,380
That's a very strong response.

136
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:49,380
Yes, because it shows maturity and willingness to learn.

137
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:53,380
Let's also talk about patience. Promotions don't always happen quickly.

138
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:56,380
That's true. Career growth takes time.

139
00:07:56,380 --> 00:08:00,380
So, a good mindset is, I'm working toward a promotion.

140
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:06,580
promotion. Exactly. That shows progress, not pressure. Now let's imagine a success

141
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:11,900
moment. You got promoted. How do you talk about it? You can say, I'm happy to share

142
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:17,100
that I was recently promoted to a senior position. Or, I've taken on a new role

143
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:22,820
with more responsibility. Yes. Then explain what changed. For example, I now

144
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:28,180
lead a team and manage project timelines. Let's also talk about feelings. How

145
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,660
How do people feel after a promotion?

146
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:33,740
Proud, excited, and sometimes nervous.

147
00:08:33,740 --> 00:08:37,140
Yes, you can say, I'm excited about the opportunity,

148
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,620
but I'm still adjusting to the new role.

149
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:42,580
Adjusting means getting used to something new.

150
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:43,780
Exactly.

151
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:46,020
This conversation is really helpful.

152
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:49,020
It shows that getting promoted is not just luck.

153
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:52,940
Yes, it's a combination of performance, communication,

154
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:55,300
mindset, and strategy.

155
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:58,180
Before we finish, let's give some final advice.

156
00:08:58,180 --> 00:08:59,180
Sure.

157
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:02,100
First, do your job well and consistently.

158
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:05,900
Second, communicate clearly and share your progress.

159
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:09,700
Third, show initiative and take on extra responsibility.

160
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:13,260
Fourth, ask for feedback and keep improving.

161
00:09:13,260 --> 00:09:17,900
And finally, talk to your manager about your goals in a professional way.

162
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:19,540
That's a complete guide.

163
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:22,700
Yes, and remember, simple English is enough.

164
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:25,140
You don't need complicated sentences.

165
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:27,980
Be clear, honest, and confident.

166
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:30,020
Now we want to hear from you.

167
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:33,460
Our question of the day is, what skill would you improve

168
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:34,700
to get promoted?

169
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:38,020
You can say, I would improve my communication skills,

170
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:40,900
or I would improve my leadership skills.

171
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:43,700
Or even, I would improve my time management

172
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,420
because I want to handle more responsibility.

173
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:48,860
Thank you so much for learning with us today.

174
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,780
Keep practicing, keep improving,

175
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,780
and keep growing in your career.

176
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:54,080
We believe in you.

177
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:56,080
See you in the next lesson. Goodbye.

178
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:27,740
and definitely not like a huge grammar monster.

179
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:33,100
Today's topic is very useful for anyone who works or wants to grow in their career.

180
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:36,140
We're talking about how to get promoted at work.

181
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:42,220
Yes, this is such an important topic because many people want to move forward in their jobs,

182
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:46,300
but they don't always know how to talk about it or what steps to take.

183
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:48,940
Exactly. You may want to say things like,

184
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:56,700
I'd like to grow in this company, or I'm ready for more responsibility, or even, what do I need to do to get promoted?

185
00:10:56,700 --> 00:11:06,260
And sometimes those conversations feel uncomfortable. Talking about career growth, salary, or promotions can feel a little stressful.

186
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:17,220
That's true. So today, we're going to help you talk about promotions in a simple and natural way, and we'll also share practical ideas that can help you move forward in your career.

187
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:22,580
And, as always, we'll keep it conversational, realistic, and easy to follow.

188
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:25,820
Alright, let's get started. Tina, how are you today?

189
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:31,620
I'm doing well, thank you. I feel focused today because I had a productive morning.

190
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:37,300
I planned my tasks, answered emails, and even had time for a quiet cup of tea.

191
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,940
That sounds very peaceful and organized.

192
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,940
I try. What about you?

193
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:45,220
I'm okay, but I had a funny moment this morning.

194
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:46,980
Oh? What happened?

195
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:49,180
I opened my notebook and wrote,

196
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:52,180
Today I will act like a future manager.

197
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:54,280
That sounds very ambitious.

198
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:58,780
Yes, but five minutes later I was eating snacks and watching videos.

199
00:11:58,780 --> 00:12:02,480
So your future manager plan changed quickly?

200
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:05,880
Very quickly. My manager version disappeared.

201
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:08,380
That's okay. Growth takes time.

202
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:10,680
Thank you. I needed that support.

203
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:14,180
Speaking of growth, today's topic is perfect.

204
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,580
Many people want to grow in their job,

205
00:12:16,580 --> 00:12:18,820
but they don't always know what to do.

206
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,740
Exactly. Some people think,

207
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,500
I work hard every day.

208
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,580
Why am I not getting promoted?

209
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:26,900
That's a very common question.

210
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:29,620
Yes, and the answer is not always simple.

211
00:12:29,620 --> 00:12:31,940
So let's start with the basics.

212
00:12:31,940 --> 00:12:34,180
What does it mean to get promoted?

213
00:12:34,180 --> 00:12:38,100
Getting promoted means moving to a higher position at work.

214
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:41,300
Usually it comes with more responsibility,

215
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:44,260
a better title, and often more pay.

216
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,460
That's the dream.

217
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:47,860
more responsibility and more money.

218
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:50,960
Yes, but also more pressure.

219
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:53,160
Ah, the hidden detail.

220
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,960
Exactly. So if someone says,

221
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:59,660
I got promoted, it means they moved to a higher role.

222
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:00,960
And you can also say,

223
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,060
I was promoted to team leader,

224
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,760
which sounds a bit more formal.

225
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:07,560
Right. Both are correct and useful.

226
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,260
Now, the big question.

227
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,860
How do you actually get promoted?

228
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:14,560
Let's start with the most important thing.

229
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:16,560
Doing your job well.

230
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:19,560
That sounds obvious, but it's very important.

231
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:23,560
Yes, you need strong performance in your current role.

232
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:30,560
So you can say, I consistently do my work well, or I focus on delivering high-quality results.

233
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:35,560
Exactly. Another useful phrase is, I consistently meet deadlines.

234
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:39,560
That means you finish your work on time again and again.

235
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:42,560
Yes, consistency is very important.

236
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:46,060
But doing your job well is not always enough, right?

237
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:52,560
That's right. If you want to get promoted, you often need to go beyond your basic responsibilities.

238
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,560
Ah, this is where initiative comes in.

239
00:13:55,560 --> 00:14:00,560
Exactly. Initiative means doing things without being told.

240
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:06,560
So I can say, I try to show initiative by helping my team and solving problems early.

241
00:14:06,560 --> 00:14:09,560
Perfect. That shows you are proactive.

242
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,560
Proactive? That's a great word.

243
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:16,560
Yes, it means you take action before problems become serious.

244
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,560
I like that. It sounds very professional.

245
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:22,560
Another important factor is communication.

246
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:25,560
Yes, communication is key in any workplace.

247
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:32,560
You can say, I communicate clearly with my team or I keep everyone updated on my progress.

248
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:35,560
I like that phrase, keep everyone updated.

249
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:38,560
It shows responsibility and teamwork.

250
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:42,560
Speaking of teamwork, that's also important for promotions, right?

251
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:46,560
Absolutely. Managers want people who work well with others.

252
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:50,560
So you can say, I enjoy collaborating with my team.

253
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:53,560
Or I support my colleagues when they need help.

254
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,560
That sounds very positive.

255
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,560
Another key idea is feedback.

256
00:14:58,560 --> 00:15:02,560
Ah yes, feedback. The thing people are sometimes afraid of.

257
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:04,560
Yes, but it's very important.

258
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:10,520
important. You can say I ask for feedback to improve my performance. That shows you want

259
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:17,560
to grow. Exactly. And you can also say I'd appreciate your feedback on how I can improve.

260
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:23,600
That sounds very polite and professional. Now let's talk about visibility. Visibility?

261
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:28,800
What does that mean? It means making sure people know about your work. So not just

262
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:36,160
working hard, but also showing your results. Exactly, but in a professional way, not by bragging.

263
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:42,400
Right, we don't want to sound arrogant. You can say, I'd like to share the results of this project.

264
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:47,280
That sounds balanced and professional. Now let's talk about career goals.

265
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,320
Yes, this is important when talking to your manager.

266
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:53,440
You can say, I'd like to grow in this company.

267
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:56,960
Or, I'm interested in taking on more responsibility.

268
00:15:56,960 --> 00:16:00,800
Another good phrase is, I'm working towards a promotion.

269
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,040
That sounds very clear and focused.

270
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:07,440
Now imagine you are talking to your manager. How can you start?

271
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:11,440
Maybe something like, I'd like to talk about my career development.

272
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:17,360
Perfect. Then you can say, I'd appreciate your feedback on what I need to improve.

273
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:20,160
That shows maturity and professionalism.

274
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:22,320
Let's give a full example.

275
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,040
Okay.

276
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:27,600
I enjoy my current role and I'm interested in growing in the company.

277
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:32,480
I'd appreciate your feedback on what I can do to move to the next level.

278
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,080
That sounds excellent.

279
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:36,560
Now let's talk about achievements.

280
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,640
Yes, this is very important.

281
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:42,960
Instead of saying, I work hard, you should give examples.

282
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:47,120
For example, I completed three major projects this quarter.

283
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:50,320
Or I helped train new team members.

284
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,440
or I improved a process to save time.

285
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:56,600
Those examples are specific and powerful.

286
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,640
Let's talk about attitude.

287
00:16:58,640 --> 00:17:01,520
A positive attitude is very important.

288
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:02,560
You can say,

289
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:06,200
I try to stay positive and solution focused.

290
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,840
Solution focused means you focus on solving problems.

291
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:13,240
So instead of complaining, you offer ideas.

292
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,240
Exactly.

293
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,400
Now let's talk about learning.

294
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,640
Learning is essential for growth.

295
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:23,120
You can say, I'm always looking for ways to improve my skills.

296
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:25,840
Or, I'm eager to learn new things.

297
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,560
That shows motivation.

298
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:29,760
Now let's talk about confidence.

299
00:17:29,760 --> 00:17:33,200
Confidence is important, but balance is key.

300
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:36,880
You can say, I believe I'm ready for more responsibility.

301
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:40,080
Or, I feel prepared for the next step.

302
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:42,560
That sounds confident, but not arrogant.

303
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:46,400
Now let's imagine success. You got promoted.

304
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,000
That's a happy moment.

305
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,500
You can say, I'm excited about this opportunity.

306
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:54,160
Or, I'm grateful for the recognition.

307
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:57,200
Or, I'm looking forward to this new role.

308
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,800
Those are great phrases.

309
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:02,200
And also, I'm still learning and adjusting.

310
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:03,800
That shows humility.

311
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:06,300
What if someone else gets promoted?

312
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:09,200
You can say, congratulations on your promotion.

313
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,300
Or, you really deserve it.

314
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,300
That sounds warm and supportive.

315
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,800
Now let's talk about patience.

316
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:18,520
Yes, promotions take time.

317
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:22,480
You can say, I understand that growth takes time.

318
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:26,020
Or I'm working toward my goals step by step.

319
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:28,000
That sounds very mature.

320
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:32,960
And if you don't get promoted, you can say, I'm focusing on improving my skills.

321
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:35,240
That's a healthy mindset.

322
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,240
Exactly.

323
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:40,920
So, Tina, if you wanted to get promoted, what would you focus on?

324
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:44,320
I would focus on communication and leadership.

325
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:48,840
I would try to support my team and improve my decision-making skills.

326
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,760
That sounds very strong.

327
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:55,320
For me, I would focus on consistency and time management.

328
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:57,480
Those are excellent areas to improve.

329
00:18:57,480 --> 00:19:00,760
I think we covered many useful ideas today.

330
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:01,760
Yes.

331
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:07,640
We talked about performance, initiative, communication, feedback, and career growth.

332
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:12,200
And we used many useful phrases that you can apply in real life.

333
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,200
Exactly.

334
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,640
Now it's your turn.

335
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:20,000
Our question of the day is, if you wanted to get promoted, what would you improve?

336
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:26,680
You can say, I would improve my communication skills, or I would work on leadership, or

337
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:29,280
I would become more organized.

338
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:31,600
Keep your answers simple and clear.

339
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:34,800
And don't worry about mistakes, just practice.

340
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:37,440
Thank you so much for learning with us today.

341
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:42,440
We hope this conversation helps you speak more confidently about your career.

342
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:46,440
However, small improvements can lead to big opportunities.

343
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:50,760
Keep practicing, stay motivated, and believe in your progress.

344
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,240
Have a wonderful day.

345
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:53,240
Take care everyone.

346
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:54,240
Goodbye.

347
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:58,560
And everyday situations that you can actually use at work and in real life.

348
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:02,480
Yes, and we always try to keep things simple, clear, and useful.

349
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:06,440
Not too formal, not too complicated, and definitely not boring.

350
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,440
Exactly.

351
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:11,720
Today's topic is something many people think about, but don't always know how to

352
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,480
talk about in English.

353
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:14,480
That's right.

354
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:17,320
Today we are talking about how to get promoted at work.

355
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:22,320
This is such an important topic because promotions are a big part of career growth.

356
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:26,880
Yes, whether you are just starting your career or already have experience, at some point

357
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:29,960
you will probably think, how can I move to the next level?

358
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:34,200
And not only that, you may need to talk about promotions with your manager, your

359
00:20:34,200 --> 00:20:36,920
coworkers, or even in job interviews.

360
00:20:36,920 --> 00:20:37,920
Exactly.

361
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:42,400
want to say things like, I'd like to grow in this company, or I'm working toward a

362
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:46,240
promotion, or I'm ready to take on more responsibility.

363
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:50,840
These are very powerful phrases, but sometimes people feel nervous using them.

364
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:53,720
Yes, especially when talking about yourself.

365
00:20:53,720 --> 00:20:58,760
It can feel a little uncomfortable to explain your achievements or ask for more responsibility.

366
00:20:58,760 --> 00:20:59,760
That's true.

367
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:03,040
So today, we're going to help you feel more confident.

368
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:06,920
We'll show you how to talk about your goals, your work, your progress, and

369
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,520
and how to position yourself for a promotion.

370
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:14,120
And we'll do it through natural conversation, with lots of practical examples you can really

371
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,120
use.

372
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:16,120
Alright, let's get started.

373
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,640
Tina, how are you today?

374
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:19,000
I'm doing well, thank you.

375
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,840
I feel very focused today.

376
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:25,880
I woke up early, made a plan for my day, and even had time to review some notes before

377
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,880
recording.

378
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:27,880
That sounds very productive.

379
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:28,960
I try.

380
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:29,960
What about you?

381
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,440
I had a very interesting morning.

382
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:32,480
Oh really, what happened?

383
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:36,640
I looked at my to-do list and decided to ignore it for 20 minutes.

384
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,440
That is not a strong start.

385
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:43,480
No, but then I came back and finished everything quickly, so technically, it worked.

386
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,200
That's one strategy, I guess.

387
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,800
Yes, I call it delayed motivation.

388
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,800
Very creative.

389
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:49,800
Thank you.

390
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:51,760
Actually, something interesting happened this week.

391
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:52,760
What is it?

392
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,960
I was talking to a friend who recently got promoted.

393
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,200
Oh, that's exciting.

394
00:21:56,200 --> 00:22:00,600
Yes, and it made me think a lot about how people move forward in their careers.

395
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,360
That's perfect for today's topic.

396
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,360
Exactly.

397
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:05,360
I asked him a lot of questions.

398
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:06,360
Like what?

399
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:09,960
what changed after the promotion, how he prepared for it,

400
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,920
and what advice he would give to someone

401
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,240
who wants to get promoted.

402
00:22:13,240 --> 00:22:14,600
That's very useful.

403
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:15,440
What did he say?

404
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:18,120
He said something very simple but powerful.

405
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,560
He said, don't wait to be noticed.

406
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,240
Show your value clearly.

407
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:24,040
That is excellent advice.

408
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:27,360
Yes, and I think that idea is very important.

409
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,760
Many people work hard,

410
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,520
but they don't always show their work in a clear way.

411
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,360
That's true.

412
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:33,800
Working hard is important,

413
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:36,480
but people also need to communicate their achievements.

414
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:37,480
Exactly.

415
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:39,400
So let's start from the beginning.

416
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,400
If someone wants to get promoted,

417
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,360
what is the first thing they should think about?

418
00:22:43,360 --> 00:22:45,600
I think the first thing is mindset.

419
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:47,280
You need to think about growth.

420
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:49,440
Growth, that's a key word.

421
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,000
Yes, you can say things like,

422
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,800
I want to grow in this company,

423
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:56,080
or I'm looking for opportunities to develop my skills.

424
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,600
That sounds very professional.

425
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:59,600
It does, and it shows that you are thinking

426
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:02,120
about the future, not just your current tasks.

427
00:23:02,120 --> 00:23:05,960
So instead of saying, I want a promotion, you can say,

428
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,840
I'd like to grow in my role.

429
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:08,640
Exactly.

430
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:10,840
It sounds more natural and less demanding.

431
00:23:10,840 --> 00:23:11,400
Good.

432
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:13,560
Now, let's talk about actions.

433
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:16,840
What should people actually do if they want a promotion?

434
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:19,280
One important thing is taking initiative.

435
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:20,680
That's a great word.

436
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,320
What does initiative mean?

437
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:24,280
Initiative means doing something helpful

438
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:25,680
without being asked.

439
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:29,200
So instead of waiting for your manager to give you tasks,

440
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,600
you look for ways to help.

441
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:31,320
Exactly.

442
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:35,240
For example, you can say, I noticed a problem, so I suggested a solution.

443
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:38,160
Or I volunteered to help with a new project.

444
00:23:38,160 --> 00:23:40,200
Yes, those are excellent examples.

445
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:43,320
Another thing people talk about is responsibility.

446
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:46,800
Right, you can say, I'm ready to take on more responsibility.

447
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,760
That's such an important phrase.

448
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:49,840
It really is.

449
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:54,720
Managers often look for people who are ready for more responsibility before giving a promotion.

450
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:57,000
So you need to show it first.

451
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:57,760
Exactly.

452
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:59,840
Let's give a real-life example.

453
00:23:59,840 --> 00:24:03,560
Imagine you are working in an office and you want a promotion.

454
00:24:03,560 --> 00:24:04,560
What can you do?

455
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:07,280
You can start by doing your current job very well.

456
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,280
That is the foundation.

457
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:09,280
Yes.

458
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:10,280
Strong performance.

459
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:14,820
Then you can look for small opportunities, for example, helping a colleague, improving

460
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:17,480
a process, or organizing a team activity.

461
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,560
I like that.

462
00:24:18,560 --> 00:24:20,720
Small actions can make a big difference.

463
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:21,720
Exactly.

464
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,480
And then you can talk about those actions.

465
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,480
Right.

466
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:26,920
Because if nobody knows, it doesn't help your career.

467
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:27,920
Yes.

468
00:24:27,920 --> 00:24:33,240
you can say in a meeting, I worked on improving a reporting system and it helped reduce errors.

469
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:35,200
That sounds very clear and professional.

470
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:36,200
Thank you.

471
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:38,860
Now, let's talk about communication with your manager.

472
00:24:38,860 --> 00:24:40,360
This is very important.

473
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:41,360
Absolutely.

474
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:44,960
If you want to get promoted, you need to talk about your goals.

475
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:47,200
Many people are afraid of that conversation.

476
00:24:47,200 --> 00:24:49,680
Yes, but it doesn't have to be scary.

477
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:50,760
You can start simply.

478
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:51,760
Like what?

479
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:55,000
You can say, I'd like to talk about my career development.

480
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,640
That's a great opening sentence.

481
00:24:56,640 --> 00:25:00,720
Or I'm interested in growing in the company and I'd like your advice.

482
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:02,800
That sounds respectful and open.

483
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:03,800
Exactly.

484
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,600
What about asking for feedback?

485
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,520
That is one of the best things you can do.

486
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:08,520
Why?

487
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:11,480
Because feedback helps you understand what you are doing well and what you need to

488
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:12,480
improve.

489
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:16,320
So you can say, I'd appreciate your feedback on my performance.

490
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:17,320
Yes.

491
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:20,360
Or what skills should I develop if I want to move to the next level?

492
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:21,880
That is very powerful.

493
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:24,640
It shows that you are serious and willing to improve.

494
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,280
Let's talk about skills.

495
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:29,120
What skills help people get promoted?

496
00:25:29,120 --> 00:25:30,120
Communication is a big one.

497
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:31,120
Definitely.

498
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:35,440
Also, time management, teamwork, problem solving, and leadership.

499
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,440
Leadership sounds important.

500
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,640
Yes, especially for higher roles.

501
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:41,000
But what if someone is not a manager yet?

502
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,560
They can still show leadership.

503
00:25:42,560 --> 00:25:43,560
How?

504
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:47,560
By helping others, sharing ideas, and taking responsibility for tasks.

505
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:50,360
So leadership is not only about position.

506
00:25:50,360 --> 00:25:51,360
Exactly.

507
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:52,560
It's also about behavior.

508
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:53,560
I like that.

509
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:54,560
Me too.

510
00:25:54,560 --> 00:25:56,260
Now, let's imagine a situation.

511
00:25:56,260 --> 00:26:00,060
Your manager asks, why do you think you are ready for a promotion?

512
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:01,660
That's a big question.

513
00:26:01,660 --> 00:26:02,660
Yes.

514
00:26:02,660 --> 00:26:03,660
What should you say?

515
00:26:03,660 --> 00:26:07,540
You can say, I believe I'm ready because I've consistently met my goals, taken on

516
00:26:07,540 --> 00:26:10,740
additional responsibilities, and supported my team.

517
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:11,740
That sounds excellent.

518
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:12,740
Thank you.

519
00:26:12,740 --> 00:26:13,740
Let me try one.

520
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:19,380
Over the past year, I've improved my performance, completed key projects, and developed new

521
00:26:19,380 --> 00:26:20,380
skills.

522
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:22,020
I feel ready for the next step.

523
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:23,020
Very good.

524
00:26:23,020 --> 00:26:24,220
That is clear and confident.

525
00:26:24,220 --> 00:26:25,220
Thank you.

526
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:26,660
promoted already.

527
00:26:26,660 --> 00:26:28,500
Not yet, but you're practicing well.

528
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:29,500
Fair enough.

529
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:31,220
Another important thing is consistency.

530
00:26:31,220 --> 00:26:32,220
What do you mean?

531
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:34,540
It's not enough to do something well one time.

532
00:26:34,540 --> 00:26:36,580
You need to perform well regularly.

533
00:26:36,580 --> 00:26:40,100
So you can say, I consistently meet deadlines.

534
00:26:40,100 --> 00:26:41,100
Exactly.

535
00:26:41,100 --> 00:26:42,940
That shows reliability.

536
00:26:42,940 --> 00:26:44,300
Reliability is a great word.

537
00:26:44,300 --> 00:26:46,500
Yes, managers trust reliable people.

538
00:26:46,500 --> 00:26:48,260
Let's talk about mistakes.

539
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:50,060
What if someone makes mistakes?

540
00:26:50,060 --> 00:26:51,140
That's normal.

541
00:26:51,140 --> 00:26:52,300
Everyone makes mistakes.

542
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:55,100
So what matters is how you handle them.

543
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:58,980
You can say, I learned from that experience and improved my approach.

544
00:26:58,980 --> 00:27:00,220
That sounds very mature.

545
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:02,340
Yes, and it shows growth.

546
00:27:02,340 --> 00:27:03,340
Growth again.

547
00:27:03,340 --> 00:27:04,340
Always growth.

548
00:27:04,340 --> 00:27:06,780
Now, let's talk about patience.

549
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:08,460
Promotions don't happen immediately.

550
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:09,460
Very true.

551
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:11,580
You can say, I understand that growth takes time.

552
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:14,380
Or I'm working toward my long-term goals.

553
00:27:14,380 --> 00:27:16,820
Yes, long-term thinking is important.

554
00:27:16,820 --> 00:27:20,940
I think many people feel frustrated when they don't get promoted quickly.

555
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:23,620
That's normal, but it's important to stay positive.

556
00:27:23,620 --> 00:27:28,500
So you can say, I didn't get promoted this time, but I'm focusing on improving.

557
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:29,500
Exactly.

558
00:27:29,500 --> 00:27:30,500
That's a strong mindset.

559
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:32,580
Let's also talk about visibility.

560
00:27:32,580 --> 00:27:33,580
Good point.

561
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:36,060
What does visibility mean in this context?

562
00:27:36,060 --> 00:27:39,140
It means people can see your work and your results.

563
00:27:39,140 --> 00:27:41,380
So not hiding in the background.

564
00:27:41,380 --> 00:27:42,380
Exactly.

565
00:27:42,380 --> 00:27:45,980
You can share updates, speak in meetings, and communicate your achievements.

566
00:27:45,980 --> 00:27:47,420
That's very important.

567
00:27:47,420 --> 00:27:51,180
Yes, because promotions often go to people whose work is visible.

568
00:27:51,180 --> 00:27:52,660
Let's give a simple example.

569
00:27:52,660 --> 00:27:53,500
Okay.

570
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:59,420
saying nothing, you can say, I completed the project ahead of schedule and improved efficiency.

571
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:01,820
Perfect. That is clear and measurable.

572
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:03,740
Now, let's talk about confidence.

573
00:28:03,740 --> 00:28:05,100
Confidence is key.

574
00:28:05,100 --> 00:28:07,100
But not too much confidence.

575
00:28:07,100 --> 00:28:08,940
Yes, balance is important.

576
00:28:08,940 --> 00:28:12,060
So you want to sound confident but not arrogant.

577
00:28:12,060 --> 00:28:17,020
Exactly. For example, I'm proud of my progress and I'm excited to continue growing.

578
00:28:17,020 --> 00:28:18,220
That's a great sentence.

579
00:28:18,220 --> 00:28:18,780
Thank you.

580
00:28:18,780 --> 00:28:22,460
All right, Leo. That was a long and very useful conversation.

581
00:28:22,460 --> 00:28:25,560
Yes, I feel like I just attended a full career workshop.

582
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:26,160
Me too.

583
00:28:26,160 --> 00:28:28,660
So let's quickly recap what we talked about.

584
00:28:28,660 --> 00:28:32,060
First, we talked about mindset and the importance of growth.

585
00:28:32,060 --> 00:28:35,860
Then we discussed taking initiative and showing responsibility.

586
00:28:35,860 --> 00:28:40,160
After that, we talked about communication with your manager and asking for feedback.

587
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:44,860
Then we covered skills like communication, leadership, and time management.

588
00:28:44,860 --> 00:28:49,560
We also talked about consistency, learning from mistakes, and staying patient.

589
00:28:49,560 --> 00:28:53,080
And finally, we discussed visibility and confidence.

590
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:53,880
Exactly.

591
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:57,720
So remember, getting promoted is not just about working hard.

592
00:28:57,720 --> 00:29:00,520
It's also about communicating your value clearly

593
00:29:00,520 --> 00:29:03,160
and showing that you are ready for more responsibility.

594
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:05,400
And you don't need complicated English.

595
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:08,360
Simple, clear, and confident phrases are enough.

596
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:10,040
Now, we want to hear from you.

597
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:11,720
Yes, this is our favorite part.

598
00:29:11,720 --> 00:29:13,640
Our question of the day is,

599
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:17,000
what skill would you improve if you wanted a promotion?

600
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,440
You can answer like this.

601
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:22,040
If I wanted a promotion, I would improve my communication skills.

602
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:26,680
Or I would improve my time management because I want to be more consistent.

603
00:29:26,680 --> 00:29:28,760
Write your answer and practice your English.

604
00:29:28,760 --> 00:29:30,680
Thank you so much for listening today.

605
00:29:30,680 --> 00:29:35,000
We hope this conversation helps you feel more confident talking about promotions.

606
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,960
Keep practicing, keep improving, and keep growing.

607
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:40,280
Have a wonderful day, evening, or night.

608
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:41,160
Take care, everyone.

609
00:29:41,160 --> 00:29:41,640
Goodbye.

610
00:29:54,460 --> 00:29:59,780
We hope you improve your English through real-life conversations, useful workplace expressions,

611
00:29:59,780 --> 00:30:02,680
and practical examples you can use immediately.

612
00:30:02,680 --> 00:30:07,940
And today's topic is very important for anyone working in a company or planning a career.

613
00:30:07,940 --> 00:30:11,080
We are talking about how to get promoted at work.

614
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:13,960
This is something many people think about every day.

615
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:19,640
A promotion means moving to a higher position, getting more responsibility, and often improving

616
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:20,800
your salary.

617
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:22,480
But it's not only about money.

618
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:27,920
It's also about recognition, growth, leadership, and proving your value over time.

619
00:30:27,920 --> 00:30:28,920
Exactly.

620
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:32,720
And many people know they want a promotion, but they don't know how to talk about it

621
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:33,880
in English.

622
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:38,720
Or how to prepare for it or even how to ask for it professionally without sounding rude

623
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:40,280
or too direct.

624
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:45,440
So today we are going to guide you step by step using natural conversations.

625
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:50,600
We'll show you how to talk about your performance, your goals, your manager conversations,

626
00:30:50,600 --> 00:30:54,480
interviews for promotion and your new role after promotion.

627
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:58,040
And we'll keep everything simple, practical, and realistic.

628
00:30:58,040 --> 00:31:02,080
So you can use these phrases in real workplaces, not just in textbooks.

629
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:04,040
Alright, Tina, let's begin.

630
00:31:04,040 --> 00:31:05,040
Let's go.

631
00:31:05,040 --> 00:31:06,940
Tina, how was your morning today?

632
00:31:06,940 --> 00:31:09,040
My morning was quite productive, actually.

633
00:31:09,040 --> 00:31:13,560
I reviewed my weekly tasks, answered emails, and planned my work priorities.

634
00:31:13,560 --> 00:31:15,360
I feel organized today.

635
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:18,640
That sounds like someone ready for a promotion already.

636
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:22,360
Maybe not yet, but I'm trying to show consistency.

637
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:25,480
Consistency is actually an important word in promotions.

638
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:30,800
Yes, managers often look at consistent performance, not just one good week.

639
00:31:30,800 --> 00:31:31,800
That's true.

640
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,840
One good day doesn't get you promoted.

641
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:34,840
Exactly.

642
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:37,680
It's about long-term performance and reliability.

643
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:40,520
Let's talk about that word, reliability.

644
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:45,040
It means people can trust you to complete your work properly and on time.

645
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:49,280
So if I always finish my tasks before deadlines, I'm reliable.

646
00:31:49,280 --> 00:31:54,040
Yes, and reliability is one of the strongest qualities for career growth.

647
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:55,040
That's useful.

648
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:59,160
So, Tina, have you ever worked in a situation where someone got promoted?

649
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,720
Yes, actually.

650
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:04,120
A colleague of mine got promoted to team leader last year.

651
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:05,500
Oh, interesting.

652
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:07,080
How did people react?

653
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:08,360
Most people were happy.

654
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:13,200
He was very hardworking and always helped others, so people felt he deserved it.

655
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:15,000
That's a very important phrase.

656
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,200
deserved it. Yes. It means the promotion was fair based on effort and performance.

657
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:27,000
So we can say he deserves the promotion because of his strong performance. Exactly.

658
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:32,680
Okay. Now let's move deeper. What exactly is a promotion in simple English?

659
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:37,440
A promotion is when you move to a higher job position with more responsibility and

660
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:42,640
usually better pay. So for example, from assistant to senior assistant.

661
00:32:42,640 --> 00:32:47,920
Yes, or from team member to team leader, or from coordinator to manager.

662
00:32:47,920 --> 00:32:48,920
I see.

663
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:51,200
So it is a step up in your career.

664
00:32:51,200 --> 00:32:54,360
Exactly, a step forward in your professional journey.

665
00:32:54,360 --> 00:32:57,600
Now, let's imagine someone wants a promotion.

666
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,200
What can they say at work?

667
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:02,400
They should never say, I want a promotion now.

668
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:03,720
That sounds too direct.

669
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:06,080
Yes, that sounds like a demand.

670
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:10,520
Instead, they can say, I'm interested in growing within the company.

671
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:12,080
That sounds much better.

672
00:33:12,080 --> 00:33:15,100
Or I would like to take on more responsibility.

673
00:33:15,100 --> 00:33:16,140
Good phrase.

674
00:33:16,140 --> 00:33:17,940
Take on more responsibility.

675
00:33:17,940 --> 00:33:21,420
Yes, it shows you are ready for bigger tasks.

676
00:33:21,420 --> 00:33:23,060
Can we make a full example?

677
00:33:23,060 --> 00:33:24,060
Sure.

678
00:33:24,060 --> 00:33:26,020
I really enjoy my current role.

679
00:33:26,020 --> 00:33:30,540
I would like to take on more responsibility and continue developing my skills within

680
00:33:30,540 --> 00:33:31,660
the company.

681
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:32,820
That sounds perfect.

682
00:33:32,820 --> 00:33:35,220
Professional, calm, and respectful.

683
00:33:35,220 --> 00:33:37,300
Now let's talk about preparation.

684
00:33:37,300 --> 00:33:39,380
How do you prepare for a promotion?

685
00:33:39,380 --> 00:33:42,860
First, you need to understand your current performance.

686
00:33:42,860 --> 00:33:44,500
Like what you've achieved?

687
00:33:44,500 --> 00:33:47,720
Yes, projects completed, deadlines met,

688
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:51,100
skills improved, teamwork contributions.

689
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:54,820
So not just I work hard, but real examples.

690
00:33:54,820 --> 00:33:57,540
Exactly, managers want evidence.

691
00:33:57,540 --> 00:33:59,820
Okay, let's create an example.

692
00:33:59,820 --> 00:34:00,740
Go ahead.

693
00:34:00,740 --> 00:34:04,500
I have completed all three major projects on time,

694
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:06,500
supported two new team members

695
00:34:06,500 --> 00:34:09,100
and consistently met all deadlines.

696
00:34:09,100 --> 00:34:11,720
That is excellent, very strong.

697
00:34:11,720 --> 00:34:13,920
It sounds more convincing than just saying,

698
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,660
I deserve a promotion.

699
00:34:15,660 --> 00:34:18,060
Yes, because it shows results.

700
00:34:18,060 --> 00:34:20,660
Now, let's imagine a manager asks,

701
00:34:20,660 --> 00:34:23,460
why do you think you are ready for a promotion?

702
00:34:23,460 --> 00:34:25,780
This is a very common question.

703
00:34:25,780 --> 00:34:27,120
How should we answer?

704
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:29,340
You can say, I believe I am ready

705
00:34:29,340 --> 00:34:32,300
because I have developed strong skills in my role

706
00:34:32,300 --> 00:34:35,480
and I'm now able to take on more responsibility.

707
00:34:35,480 --> 00:34:38,140
That sounds confident, but not arrogant.

708
00:34:38,140 --> 00:34:41,980
Exactly. Confidence is good, arrogance is not.

709
00:34:41,980 --> 00:34:43,740
What does arrogant mean?

710
00:34:43,740 --> 00:34:47,940
It means you think you are better than others in a rude or proud way.

711
00:34:47,940 --> 00:34:52,340
Let's talk about feelings. How do people feel when they want a promotion?

712
00:34:52,340 --> 00:34:58,300
Many emotions. Excited, nervous, motivated, and sometimes uncertain.

713
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:00,340
Uncertain means not sure, right?

714
00:35:00,340 --> 00:35:04,220
Yes. For example, I'm not sure if I'm ready yet.

715
00:35:04,220 --> 00:35:05,420
That's very common.

716
00:35:05,420 --> 00:35:07,980
Yes. Many people doubt themselves.

717
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:09,900
What is a good phrase for that?

718
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:15,260
You can say, I'm still developing my skills, but I feel I'm moving in the right direction.

719
00:35:15,260 --> 00:35:16,260
That's a good balance.

720
00:35:16,260 --> 00:35:18,940
Yes, it shows growth mindset.

721
00:35:18,940 --> 00:35:22,060
Now let's talk about speaking to your manager.

722
00:35:22,060 --> 00:35:23,820
Very important situation.

723
00:35:23,820 --> 00:35:25,960
How should you start the conversation?

724
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:29,540
You can say, I'd like to talk about my career development.

725
00:35:29,540 --> 00:35:31,620
That sounds serious, but polite.

726
00:35:31,620 --> 00:35:36,580
Yes, or I would appreciate your feedback on my performance.

727
00:35:36,580 --> 00:35:38,140
Work is a key word here.

728
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:42,180
Yes, it means advice and evaluation of your work.

729
00:35:42,180 --> 00:35:47,660
So the conversation is not only asking for promotion, but also asking for improvement.

730
00:35:47,660 --> 00:35:48,660
Exactly.

731
00:35:48,660 --> 00:35:50,500
That shows professionalism.

732
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:52,980
Let's build a full conversation example.

733
00:35:52,980 --> 00:35:53,980
Good idea.

734
00:35:53,980 --> 00:35:56,300
Manager, how are things going?

735
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:58,220
Employee, things are going well.

736
00:35:58,220 --> 00:36:02,900
I've been focusing on improving my performance and taking on more responsibility.

737
00:36:02,900 --> 00:36:05,740
Manager, do you have any goals?

738
00:36:05,740 --> 00:36:11,420
Yes, I would like to grow within the company and work toward a promotion in the future.

739
00:36:11,420 --> 00:36:14,060
Manager, what do you think you need?

740
00:36:14,060 --> 00:36:19,260
Employee, I would appreciate your feedback on what skills I should improve to move to

741
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,580
the next level.

742
00:36:20,580 --> 00:36:22,460
That is a perfect conversation.

743
00:36:22,460 --> 00:36:26,020
Yes, it's natural, respectful and professional.

744
00:36:26,020 --> 00:36:29,300
Now let's talk about when you actually get promoted.

745
00:36:29,300 --> 00:36:30,740
The best moment.

746
00:36:30,740 --> 00:36:31,740
What can you say?

747
00:36:31,740 --> 00:36:36,060
Thank you for the opportunity. I really appreciate the trust you've placed in me.

748
00:36:36,060 --> 00:36:37,900
That sounds very polite.

749
00:36:37,900 --> 00:36:40,540
Yes, gratitude is very important.

750
00:36:40,540 --> 00:36:42,460
Can we add more examples?

751
00:36:42,460 --> 00:36:43,180
Sure.

752
00:36:43,180 --> 00:36:48,220
I am very happy about the promotion. I'm excited to take on new responsibilities and

753
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:50,380
continue contributing to the team.

754
00:36:50,380 --> 00:36:56,620
Very good. And maybe also, I will do my best to meet expectations in my new role.

755
00:36:56,620 --> 00:37:00,860
Perfect. Now let's talk about challenges after promotion.

756
00:37:00,860 --> 00:37:03,500
Yes, because it's not always easy.

757
00:37:03,500 --> 00:37:05,900
More responsibility, more pressure.

758
00:37:05,900 --> 00:37:06,780
Exactly.

759
00:37:06,780 --> 00:37:10,420
You might say, I'm still adjusting to my new workload.

760
00:37:10,420 --> 00:37:12,980
Adjusting means getting used to something.

761
00:37:12,980 --> 00:37:13,860
Yes.

762
00:37:13,860 --> 00:37:14,980
Another phrase?

763
00:37:14,980 --> 00:37:18,260
It's a learning process, but I'm improving every day.

764
00:37:18,260 --> 00:37:20,660
Tina, what is the most important advice

765
00:37:20,660 --> 00:37:21,940
for getting promoted?

766
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:25,820
Be consistent, show initiative, communicate well,

767
00:37:25,820 --> 00:37:27,620
and take responsibility.

768
00:37:27,620 --> 00:37:30,700
Initiative means doing things without being told.

769
00:37:30,700 --> 00:37:33,740
Exactly. That is very valuable at work.

770
00:37:33,740 --> 00:37:37,100
So promotion is not luck, it is preparation.

771
00:37:37,100 --> 00:37:39,580
Yes, and performance over time.

772
00:37:39,580 --> 00:37:41,180
Let's summarize everything.

773
00:37:41,180 --> 00:37:42,000
Sure.

774
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:44,860
To get promoted, you need strong performance.

775
00:37:44,860 --> 00:37:46,940
You need clear communication.

776
00:37:46,940 --> 00:37:49,980
You need to show responsibility and initiative.

777
00:37:49,980 --> 00:37:53,140
And you need to speak professionally about your goals.

778
00:37:53,140 --> 00:37:54,140
Perfect.

779
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:56,580
And remember, growth takes time.

780
00:37:56,580 --> 00:37:58,940
Before we finish, our question for listeners

781
00:37:58,940 --> 00:38:02,540
is, what skill would you improve to get promoted?

782
00:38:02,540 --> 00:38:07,260
Maybe communication, leadership, confidence, or time management?

783
00:38:07,260 --> 00:38:09,100
Write your answer in the comments.

784
00:38:09,100 --> 00:38:11,580
And keep practicing English with us every day.

785
00:38:11,580 --> 00:38:14,340
Thanks for listening to the Business English Podcast.

786
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:15,780
We'll see you in the next lesson.

787
00:38:15,780 --> 00:38:16,780
Goodbye.

788
00:38:16,780 --> 00:38:17,780
Hi, everyone.

789
00:38:17,780 --> 00:38:18,780
Welcome back.

790
00:38:18,780 --> 00:38:20,720
We're really happy you're here with us today.

791
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:26,180
On this podcast, we help you learn natural, practical English through real conversations,

792
00:38:26,180 --> 00:38:29,980
clear explanations and everyday work situations.

793
00:38:29,980 --> 00:38:31,340
Exactly.

794
00:38:31,340 --> 00:38:37,340
We want English to feel simple, useful, and something you can actually use in your daily

795
00:38:37,340 --> 00:38:38,340
life.

796
00:38:38,340 --> 00:38:40,900
Not something complicated or stressful.

797
00:38:40,900 --> 00:38:45,260
And today's topic is something many people think about but don't always know how to

798
00:38:45,260 --> 00:38:46,900
talk about in English.

799
00:38:46,900 --> 00:38:47,900
Yes.

800
00:38:47,900 --> 00:38:52,660
Today we're talking about how to get promoted at work, and more importantly, how to talk

801
00:38:52,660 --> 00:38:55,540
about it in clear, natural English.

802
00:38:55,540 --> 00:39:00,900
This is a very important topic because promotions are a big part of professional life.

803
00:39:00,900 --> 00:39:01,980
Definitely.

804
00:39:01,980 --> 00:39:07,460
You might want a promotion, you might be preparing for one, or maybe you just got promoted and

805
00:39:07,460 --> 00:39:09,740
need to explain your new role.

806
00:39:09,740 --> 00:39:14,660
Or maybe your manager asks about your goals and you want to answer in a confident and

807
00:39:14,660 --> 00:39:16,260
professional way.

808
00:39:16,260 --> 00:39:17,260
Exactly.

809
00:39:17,260 --> 00:39:22,420
So today, we'll help you talk about all of that, your goals, your progress, your

810
00:39:22,420 --> 00:39:25,940
skills and how to move forward in your career.

811
00:39:25,940 --> 00:39:32,620
We'll also share practical phrases, real examples, and honest situations that happen in the workplace.

812
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:36,820
And we'll keep everything simple, natural, and easy to follow.

813
00:39:36,820 --> 00:39:41,900
So if you enjoy learning with us, don't forget to subscribe and follow the podcast.

814
00:39:41,900 --> 00:39:43,580
And now let's get started.

815
00:39:43,580 --> 00:39:45,460
Tina, how are you today?

816
00:39:45,460 --> 00:39:47,060
I'm doing well, thank you.

817
00:39:47,060 --> 00:39:49,260
I feel quite motivated today.

818
00:39:49,260 --> 00:39:53,620
I actually started my morning by writing down my goals for the week.

819
00:39:53,620 --> 00:39:55,580
That sounds very productive.

820
00:39:55,580 --> 00:39:57,700
What kind of goals did you write?

821
00:39:57,700 --> 00:39:59,380
Mostly work-related goals.

822
00:39:59,380 --> 00:40:07,020
I wrote things like finish reports on time, improve communication, and take more initiative.

823
00:40:07,020 --> 00:40:08,500
Take more initiative?

824
00:40:08,500 --> 00:40:11,420
That already sounds like someone who wants a promotion.

825
00:40:11,420 --> 00:40:12,420
Exactly.

826
00:40:12,420 --> 00:40:16,740
I think many people want to grow at work, but they don't always know how to show

827
00:40:16,740 --> 00:40:17,740
it.

828
00:40:17,740 --> 00:40:19,020
That's very true.

829
00:40:19,020 --> 00:40:21,340
What about you, Leo? How was your morning?

830
00:40:21,340 --> 00:40:23,920
My morning was... interesting.

831
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:26,880
Interesting? That sounds dangerous.

832
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:31,960
I tried to be productive. I opened my laptop, made coffee, and told myself,

833
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:35,240
Today I will act like a future manager.

834
00:40:35,240 --> 00:40:37,000
That sounds like a strong start.

835
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:40,840
Yes, but then I spent 20 minutes choosing a playlist.

836
00:40:40,840 --> 00:40:44,280
So not very managerial behavior.

837
00:40:44,280 --> 00:40:46,560
Not yet, but I'm working toward it.

838
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:51,320
And that phrase, working toward it, is actually very important for today's topic.

839
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:55,360
Yes, because getting promoted is not something that happens suddenly.

840
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:57,000
It's usually a process.

841
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Exactly.

842
00:40:58,000 --> 00:41:00,520
So, let's start with a basic question.

843
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:02,480
What does it mean to get promoted?

844
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:06,600
To get promoted means to move to a higher position at work.

845
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:08,720
Usually with more responsibility.

846
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:13,080
And often with a higher salary, although not always immediately.

847
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:14,080
Right.

848
00:41:14,080 --> 00:41:17,780
When someone gets promoted, their role usually changes.

849
00:41:17,780 --> 00:41:22,680
Yes, they may have to lead a team, make decisions, or manage projects.

850
00:41:22,680 --> 00:41:27,400
So if someone asks, how can I get promoted, what's the simple answer?

851
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:32,360
The simple answer is, you need to show that you are ready for more responsibility.

852
00:41:32,360 --> 00:41:36,320
That sounds simple, but in reality, it involves many things.

853
00:41:36,320 --> 00:41:42,240
Yes, it involves performance, communication, attitude, and consistency.

854
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:44,460
Let's talk about performance first.

855
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:47,020
What does strong performance mean?

856
00:41:47,020 --> 00:41:52,440
Strong performance means doing your job well, meeting deadlines, completing tasks, and producing

857
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:53,680
good results.

858
00:41:53,680 --> 00:41:58,880
So if I say, I consistently meet my deadlines, that sounds strong.

859
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:00,280
Very strong.

860
00:42:00,280 --> 00:42:02,320
Consistency is very important.

861
00:42:02,320 --> 00:42:07,960
Because doing something well once is good, but doing it well every time is better.

862
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:09,280
Exactly.

863
00:42:09,280 --> 00:42:13,720
look for people who are reliable over time. Let's give an example.

864
00:42:13,720 --> 00:42:19,680
Sure, someone could say, over the past six months I've consistently completed my tasks

865
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:23,360
on time and supported my team during busy periods.

866
00:42:23,360 --> 00:42:25,400
That sounds very professional.

867
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:29,880
Yes, and it shows real results, not just general statements.

868
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:34,400
Now let's talk about another important factor, initiative.

869
00:42:34,400 --> 00:42:36,900
Initiative is a key part of getting promoted.

870
00:42:36,900 --> 00:42:39,240
What does initiative mean?

871
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:42,440
Initiative means doing helpful things without being told.

872
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:46,160
So, instead of waiting for instructions, you take action.

873
00:42:46,160 --> 00:42:47,160
Exactly.

874
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:52,080
For example, if you see a problem and try to solve it, that shows initiative.

875
00:42:52,080 --> 00:42:53,980
Let me try an example.

876
00:42:53,980 --> 00:42:58,780
I try to show initiative by helping my team and solving problems early.

877
00:42:58,780 --> 00:43:00,340
That's excellent.

878
00:43:00,340 --> 00:43:02,420
Very natural and professional.

879
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:05,380
Now let's talk about communication.

880
00:43:05,380 --> 00:43:09,220
Communication is extremely important, especially for higher roles.

881
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:12,380
Because when you get promoted, you often work with more people.

882
00:43:12,380 --> 00:43:17,980
Yes, and you may need to explain ideas, give instructions, and provide feedback.

883
00:43:17,980 --> 00:43:23,060
So someone could say, I'm working on improving my communication skills so I can take on more

884
00:43:23,060 --> 00:43:24,060
responsibility.

885
00:43:24,060 --> 00:43:25,260
Perfect.

886
00:43:25,260 --> 00:43:27,460
That shows awareness and effort.

887
00:43:27,460 --> 00:43:30,160
Now let's talk about attitude.

888
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:34,020
Attitude is how you approach your work, your mindset, and behavior.

889
00:43:34,020 --> 00:43:38,500
So being positive, responsible, and open to learning is important.

890
00:43:38,500 --> 00:43:43,500
Yes, managers often promote people who are easy to work with and willing to grow.

891
00:43:43,500 --> 00:43:49,500
Let's imagine a situation. Someone wants a promotion. What can they say to their manager?

892
00:43:49,500 --> 00:43:53,500
They could say, I'd like to talk about my career development.

893
00:43:53,500 --> 00:43:55,500
That sounds polite and professional.

894
00:43:55,500 --> 00:44:02,500
Yes, and then they can continue, I'm interested in growing in the company and taking on more responsibility.

895
00:44:02,500 --> 00:44:05,500
That's much better than saying, I want a promotion now.

896
00:44:05,500 --> 00:44:08,500
Definitely. The tone is very important.

897
00:44:08,500 --> 00:44:14,500
Tone means how your words feel, whether they sound respectful, confident or aggressive.

898
00:44:14,500 --> 00:44:17,500
Exactly. Now let's build a full example.

899
00:44:17,500 --> 00:44:23,560
Okay. I enjoy my current role and I'm interested in growing in the company.

900
00:44:23,560 --> 00:44:27,560
I'd appreciate your feedback on how I can prepare for the next step.

901
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:30,560
That's excellent. Calm, clear, and professional.

902
00:44:30,560 --> 00:44:33,560
Now let's talk about preparation.

903
00:44:33,560 --> 00:44:36,560
Before asking for a promotion, what should you do?

904
00:44:36,560 --> 00:44:39,560
You should prepare examples of your work.

905
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:43,560
Yes, examples of achievements, projects, and contributions.

906
00:44:43,560 --> 00:44:46,560
Because saying, I work hard is not enough.

907
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:49,560
Exactly. You need to be specific.

908
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:52,560
For example, I completed three major projects,

909
00:44:52,560 --> 00:44:56,560
helped train new team members, and improved our workflow.

910
00:44:56,560 --> 00:44:58,560
That sounds much stronger.

911
00:44:58,560 --> 00:45:00,560
Now let's talk about responsibility.

912
00:45:00,560 --> 00:45:06,060
Responsibility means tasks or duties you're expected to handle.

913
00:45:06,060 --> 00:45:09,240
And when you get promoted, your responsibilities increase.

914
00:45:09,240 --> 00:45:14,800
Yes, you may need to manage people, make decisions, or lead projects.

915
00:45:14,800 --> 00:45:19,400
So a good phrase is, I'm ready to take on more responsibility.

916
00:45:19,400 --> 00:45:21,960
That's one of the best phrases for this topic.

917
00:45:21,960 --> 00:45:24,680
Now let's talk about leadership.

918
00:45:24,680 --> 00:45:27,840
Leadership means guiding or managing others.

919
00:45:27,840 --> 00:45:31,800
Not everyone starts as a leader, but they can develop leadership skills.

920
00:45:31,800 --> 00:45:36,640
Yes, and you can say, I'm working on developing my leadership skills.

921
00:45:36,640 --> 00:45:38,760
That shows growth and ambition.

922
00:45:38,760 --> 00:45:39,760
Exactly.

923
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:42,840
Speaking of ambition, what does that mean?

924
00:45:42,840 --> 00:45:46,720
Ambition means a strong desire to succeed and improve.

925
00:45:46,720 --> 00:45:51,680
So if I say, I'm ambitious, but I also want to learn, that sounds balanced.

926
00:45:51,680 --> 00:45:53,560
Yes, very good balance.

927
00:45:53,560 --> 00:45:56,440
Now, let's imagine someone gets promoted.

928
00:45:56,440 --> 00:45:57,960
How can they describe it?

929
00:45:57,960 --> 00:46:02,360
They can explain their old role, their new role, and what changed.

930
00:46:02,360 --> 00:46:03,440
For example?

931
00:46:03,440 --> 00:46:08,400
For example, I was promoted from assistant to team supervisor.

932
00:46:08,400 --> 00:46:10,800
Before I handled customer requests.

933
00:46:10,800 --> 00:46:14,520
Now I also manage schedules and support my team.

934
00:46:14,520 --> 00:46:16,760
That's clear and easy to understand.

935
00:46:16,760 --> 00:46:19,480
Now let's talk about challenges.

936
00:46:19,480 --> 00:46:21,160
Promotions are not always easy.

937
00:46:21,160 --> 00:46:23,600
Yes, they come with pressure.

938
00:46:23,600 --> 00:46:25,200
And a bigger workload.

939
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:29,840
So someone might say, I'm excited about the promotion, but I'm still adjusting to the

940
00:46:29,840 --> 00:46:31,240
new workload.

941
00:46:31,240 --> 00:46:33,200
That sounds honest and realistic.

942
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:37,680
Now, let's talk about what happens if someone does not get promoted.

943
00:46:37,680 --> 00:46:39,040
That's also important.

944
00:46:39,040 --> 00:46:44,560
They can say, I didn't get the promotion this time, but I'm focusing on improving my skills.

945
00:46:44,560 --> 00:46:46,640
That's a very healthy response.

946
00:46:46,640 --> 00:46:51,320
And they can also say, I asked for feedback so I can do better next time.

947
00:46:51,320 --> 00:46:52,320
Excellent.

948
00:46:52,320 --> 00:46:57,480
feedback helps you understand what to improve. Exactly. Now let's talk about

949
00:46:57,480 --> 00:47:03,720
daily habits that help you get promoted. Good idea. First, being consistent. Second,

950
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:10,280
communicating clearly. Third, helping others. And fourth, learning continuously. So

951
00:47:10,280 --> 00:47:15,120
someone could say, I try to improve every day and support my team. Perfect.

952
00:47:15,120 --> 00:47:20,160
Now let's talk about confidence. Confidence is very important but it

953
00:47:20,160 --> 00:47:22,280
It should not become arrogance.

954
00:47:22,280 --> 00:47:27,880
So instead of saying, I deserve a promotion now, you can say, I believe I'm ready for

955
00:47:27,880 --> 00:47:29,240
the next step.

956
00:47:29,240 --> 00:47:30,240
Much better.

957
00:47:30,240 --> 00:47:33,080
Now let's give a full conversation example.

958
00:47:33,080 --> 00:47:34,080
Good idea.

959
00:47:34,080 --> 00:47:37,160
Manager, what are your career goals?

960
00:47:37,160 --> 00:47:42,320
Employee, I'd like to grow within the company and take on more responsibility.

961
00:47:42,320 --> 00:47:43,840
Manager, that's great.

962
00:47:43,840 --> 00:47:45,600
What have you been working on?

963
00:47:45,600 --> 00:47:51,600
I've been focusing on improving my performance, meeting deadlines, and supporting my team.

964
00:47:51,600 --> 00:47:53,600
Manager, that's good progress.

965
00:47:53,600 --> 00:47:58,600
Employee, I'd appreciate your feedback on how I can prepare for a promotion.

966
00:47:58,600 --> 00:48:01,600
That's a very strong and natural conversation.

967
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:04,600
Now, let's talk about long-term thinking.

968
00:48:04,600 --> 00:48:06,600
Promotions don't happen overnight.

969
00:48:06,600 --> 00:48:09,600
Yes, you need patience and effort.

970
00:48:09,600 --> 00:48:13,600
So you can say, I'm working toward a promotion step-by-step.

971
00:48:13,600 --> 00:48:14,600
That shows maturity.

972
00:48:14,600 --> 00:48:18,600
Now, let's reflect. What are the key things to remember?

973
00:48:18,600 --> 00:48:23,600
Work well, communicate clearly, show initiative, and be consistent.

974
00:48:23,600 --> 00:48:27,600
And speak professionally when discussing your goals.

975
00:48:27,600 --> 00:48:28,600
Exactly.

976
00:48:28,600 --> 00:48:30,600
Now, we want to hear from you.

977
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:32,600
Yes, this is our favorite part.

978
00:48:32,600 --> 00:48:35,600
If you wanted to get promoted, what skill would you improve?

979
00:48:35,600 --> 00:48:42,600
You can say, I would improve my communication skills, or I would improve my leadership skills.

980
00:48:42,600 --> 00:48:45,560
or I would improve my time management.

981
00:48:45,560 --> 00:48:48,000
Write your answer and practice your English.

982
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:50,440
Thank you so much for learning with us today.

983
00:48:50,440 --> 00:48:53,640
We hope this conversation helps you speak more confidently

984
00:48:53,640 --> 00:48:54,880
about your career.

985
00:48:54,880 --> 00:48:58,440
Remember, simple and clear English is powerful.

986
00:48:58,440 --> 00:49:01,800
Keep practicing, keep improving, and keep growing.

987
00:49:01,800 --> 00:49:05,560
Have a wonderful day, evening, or night wherever you are.

988
00:49:05,560 --> 00:49:06,400
And...
